WEBVTT

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.850
SEN HATSUMI
REP. FIGHTER OF NOGI GROUP

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.600
Who the hell are you?

00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.020
Me?

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.230
I am a "becomer."

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.520
People call me...

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.480
"The Faceless Man."

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.400
"The Faceless Man?"

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:35.030
Sounds pretty cheap if you ask me.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.120
Besides, I can see your face very clearly.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.660
Oh?

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.920
Are you sure you can?

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:46.870
Wait. That's...

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:48.420
TADASHI IIDA - GAOLAN WONGSAWAT

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.460
Is that me?

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:51.420
What?

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.800
JERRY TYSON

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.300
<i>It's exactly like Gaolan's move.</i>

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.470
<i>It's not just for show.</i>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:01.430
<i>So, his style is boxing.</i>

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:04.430
Don't get me wrong.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:08.650
I can become... more than just a boxer.

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:09.730
NAOYA OHKUBO

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.070
That's my style!

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:13.490
So? Surprised, aren't you?

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:16.610
<i>Even his tone and mood changed.</i>

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:20.580
I'll tell you my secret.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.830
I'm an actor...

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:24.580
TAKAYUKI CHIBA
YOSHITAKE REAL ESTATE

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:25.870
...of the underground.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.630
<i>There are people called "actors"</i>
<i>in the underworld.</i>

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:36.880
<i>They play completely different people</i>
<i>to perpetrate scams and other crimes.</i>

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.890
<i>I've heard that...</i>

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.310
<i>some underworld actors</i>
<i>specialize in fighting scenes.</i>

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.520
<i>I guess this guy's</i>
<i>one of those militant actors.</i>

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.070
I can copy any action perfectly
after seeing it once.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:57.530
So far, 22 fighters have competed
in this tournament

00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:03.660
and I've seen the public fights
of Gaolan Wongsawat and Naoya Ohkubo.

00:02:04.160 --> 00:02:08.330
I have mastered
a total of 24 fighting styles.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.750
In other words,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:14.050
<i>I can punch like Gaolan,</i>
<i>wrestle like Sekibayashi,</i>

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:16.550
<i>and ground grapple like Cosmo Imai.</i>

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.680
Do you understand?

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.680
Your opponent is not Takayuki Chiba.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:27.350
It's a chimera of 24 fighters.

00:03:59.030 --> 00:04:03.950
"ODDITIES"

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:10.740
I appreciate Mr. Yoshitake scheduling
my match later in the tournament.

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:12.580
YOSHIRO YOSHITAKE
YOSHITAKE REAL ESTATE

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:17.380
The more matches there are before mine,
the more fighters I can trace.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:21.840
As this tournament moves forward,
I become stronger.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.010
You're a copycat counting your chickens
before they hatch?

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:28.680
That's not even funny.

00:04:29.430 --> 00:04:30.970
Take your stance, underling.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:34.560
Use other people's power
as much as you want.

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:39.070
<i>Chiba has told two lies.</i>

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:44.450
<i>One, he can only trace movements</i>
<i>and techniques of the target.</i>

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:46.530
<i>He cannot copy physical abilities</i>

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:51.240
<i>such as Kure Family's Release</i>
<i>or Lihito's Razor's Edge.</i>

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:54.120
<i>And, even if he imitates</i>
<i>a technique perfectly,</i>

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:58.130
<i>its power is only proportional</i>
<i>to Chiba's physical abilities.</i>

00:04:58.840 --> 00:05:04.300
<i>Two, at this point, he has traced</i>
<i>24 fighters' movements,</i>

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:08.510
<i>but is barely able to use any of them</i>
<i>in an actual battle.</i>

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:11.680
<i>Still, it is enough.</i>

00:05:12.350 --> 00:05:13.430
<i>In Hatsumi's eyes,</i>

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:20.690
<i>Takayuki Chiba appears to be</i>
<i>a larger monster than he really is.</i>

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:25.070
<i>A man who can use any move</i>
<i>he's seen once.</i>

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:27.070
Are you ready?

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:31.950
<i>By the next round, I'll have finished</i>
<i>committing the fighters' moves to memory,</i>

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:35.830
<i>to use them in an actual match.</i>

00:05:37.080 --> 00:05:42.630
<i>I'll fight with the styles I've stolen</i>
<i>from other martial artists for today.</i>

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:47.050
Here we go, Sen Hatsumi.

00:05:47.510 --> 00:05:49.300
Oh! That stance!

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:52.140
<i>That's Andrews Filho.</i>

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:54.850
<i>He was the strongest Kidokan karate master</i>

00:05:54.930 --> 00:05:57.980
<i>who could kill anyone with just one punch.</i>

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:01.610
<i>You can even copy a dead man?</i>

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.740
<i>I guess I don't need to pull my punches.</i>

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.080
Match over! We have a winner!

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.540
<i>Twenty-six seconds</i>
<i>after the start of the match,</i>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:23.380
<i>it was all over.</i>

00:06:25.960 --> 00:06:26.880
Fight!

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:02.670
Gathering Clouds: Triple Strike.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:04.790
Time to go to sleep,

00:07:05.170 --> 00:07:06.710
copycat.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.930
Match is over! We have a winner!

00:07:11.890 --> 00:07:14.680
<i>It... It's over!</i>

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:19.230
<i>The winner of the 13th match is</i>
<i>Sen Hatsumi, a.k.a. the Floating Cloud.</i>

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:23.100
<i>It took only 26 seconds</i>
<i>for him to win the match.</i>

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:25.230
<i>Sen Hatsumi is so strong!</i>

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:29.400
That man made a wrong choice.

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:30.490
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.740
-What?
-His last move was an aikido technique.

00:07:32.860 --> 00:07:33.820
JUN SEKIBAYASHI

00:07:33.910 --> 00:07:34.990
It was a bad move.

00:07:35.990 --> 00:07:41.160
<i>Sen's fighting style is based on</i>
<i>his own style, the Hatsumi-style aikido.</i>

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.090
It was reckless of him
to fight against it with aikido.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.130
He's just a knockoff, after all.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:53.890
Just a single mistake
can cost you everything.

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:55.140
That is...

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.720
what a kengan match is.

00:07:59.220 --> 00:08:00.390
Well, well.

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:02.170
HIDEKI NOGI
CHAIRMAN OF NOGI GROUP

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.970
What does a loser want from me,

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:05.520
Mr. Yoshitake?

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.020
Don't get big-headed.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:10.530
This isn't over yet!

00:08:10.690 --> 00:08:14.280
I'm going to take you down one day.

00:08:15.490 --> 00:08:18.540
You are pretty easygoing, aren't you?

00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:22.620
It seems you don't fully understand
the situation you are in.

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:23.750
Huh?

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:28.210
I heard you committed physical violence
before the match.

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.510
Don't play the fool with me.
I know you sent your assassin to me.

00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:35.760
I suppose you wanted to threaten me,
but too bad for you.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:38.010
<i>It didn't work out that way.</i>

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:41.180
Don't get carried away,
just because you won the match.

00:08:41.270 --> 00:08:43.060
I'm going to get testimony from him

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.900
and disqualify Nogi Group
from the tournament.

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:49.320
Oh, are you sure you want to do that?

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:55.410
If you do, you'll lose
your Kengan Association membership.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:56.450
Huh?

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.620
Actually, the man
you ordered your man to assault...

00:09:00.370 --> 00:09:04.410
<i>just became</i>
<i>a Kengan Association member yesterday.</i>

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.580
<i>I recommended him.</i>

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:07.630
Wha...

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:10.840
As you know, Mr. Yoshitake,

00:09:11.590 --> 00:09:14.260
personal fights between members
are strictly prohibited.

00:09:14.470 --> 00:09:16.300
If this comes to light,

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:21.970
Yoshitake Real Estate will be
eliminated from the association for good.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.810
So, this is what you wanted, isn't it?

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:28.100
You were trying to set me up all along

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:30.940
and made me fight that guy.

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.360
Oh, come on. That's disgraceful.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:39.700
All I did was recommend him
for the Kengan Association membership.

00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:42.370
Why, Nogi? I don't understand.

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:47.540
You could've just made me forfeit
if you'd planned all that.

00:09:47.960 --> 00:09:52.300
That would've better
conserved Hatsumi's energy, too.

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:53.630
Why?

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:57.760
You don't know a thing.

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.050
Fighters are no more than our pawns.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:06.810
You need to watch them fight
to see which pawn is stronger.

00:10:07.350 --> 00:10:12.650
If Sen had lost to Chiba, I would have
supported Yoshitake Real Estate

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:17.070
with all of the might of Nogi Group.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.820
Even if you had won the tournament,

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:26.200
I would have made you designate me
as the association's chairman.

00:10:28.500 --> 00:10:30.790
Remember this, boy.

00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:34.630
I am in a different class than you.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:40.890
Let's welcome the fighters
for the 14th match!

00:10:41.890 --> 00:10:44.310
<i>Some call him "Murder Physician."</i>

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.640
<i>Some call him "Doctor Death."</i>

00:10:48.020 --> 00:10:52.610
<i>The doctor draped in death</i>
<i>made an emergency visit to the tournament.</i>

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.650
<i>He leads his poor patients to hell.</i>

00:10:57.030 --> 00:11:00.450
<i>The gate to hell is about to open.</i>

00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:04.580
<i>Standing at 174 cm and weighing 62 kg,</i>

00:11:04.700 --> 00:11:07.410
<i>he makes his kengan match debut today.</i>

00:11:07.620 --> 00:11:09.910
Representing the University of Teito,

00:11:10.250 --> 00:11:16.050
<i>also known as the Dissector,</i>
<i>Hajime Hanafusa!</i>

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:21.010
HAJIME HANAFUSA

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.720
I love this place.

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.220
The smell of death is filling the air.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.480
YUKIO DAZAI
PRESIDENT OF UNIVERSITY OF TEITO

00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:34.560
Next up is another incredible assassin.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:39.650
<i>A bare-handed serial killer, the likes</i>
<i>of which had never been seen</i>

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:42.320
<i>in Japanese criminal history.</i>

00:11:42.570 --> 00:11:45.330
<i>He was a medical student back then,</i>

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:49.620
<i>and now, after 30 years,</i>
<i>the killer has returned.</i>

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:53.880
<i>Standing at 201 cm and weighing 147 kg,</i>

00:11:54.000 --> 00:11:56.790
<i>he makes his kengan match debut today.</i>

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:01.930
Representing Juoh Communications,
also known as the Bloody Tusk,

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:06.220
Yohei Bando!

00:12:10.430 --> 00:12:12.270
YOHEI BANDO
JUOH COMMUNICATIONS

00:12:12.350 --> 00:12:16.110
Good grief. It's so raucous outside.

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:19.780
<i>Hanafusa,</i>

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:23.950
<i>don't forget your duty.</i>

00:12:24.910 --> 00:12:26.370
<i>This is very sudden,</i>

00:12:26.450 --> 00:12:31.290
<i>but Hanafusa is an agent</i>
<i>sent by the Japanese government.</i>

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.850
<i>Yohei Bando is a death row inmate.</i>

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:37.500
<i>The government allowed him</i>
<i>to take part in the tournament</i>

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.960
<i>to secretly get rid of him.</i>

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:45.300
<i>His first execution</i>
<i>took place 25 years ago.</i>

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:50.970
<i>However, he survived</i>
<i>the 90-minute-long execution.</i>

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:57.610
<i>The execution order was issued every time</i>
<i>a new Minister of Justice was inaugurated,</i>

00:12:57.940 --> 00:13:02.740
<i>but he survived all 45 executions.</i>

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:06.990
<i>He has been waiting for 25 years</i>
<i>to get his death penalty fulfilled.</i>

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:12.500
<i>The only method of execution</i>
<i>allowed in this country is hanging.</i>

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.670
<i>A death row inmate who cannot</i>
<i>be hanged to death</i>

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.130
<i>means the defeat of the law.</i>

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:20.500
MINISTRY OF JUSTICE

00:13:20.960 --> 00:13:22.790
SEISUKE TAKADA
PRES. JUOH COMMUNICATIONS

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:25.920
<i>The country allows him to fight</i>
<i>then sends an assassin to face him.</i>

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:28.930
<i>Well, I expected as much.</i>

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:33.680
I got a smaller opponent than I expected.

00:13:34.310 --> 00:13:36.850
Now, I wonder what to do with you.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:39.400
A man that can't be killed by hanging.

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:41.150
That's tempting.

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.360
I would love to dissect you.

00:13:44.860 --> 00:13:49.660
Seems like you don't live a decent life.

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.950
But who am I to talk?

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:55.150
<i>Those eyes...</i>

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:56.910
OHMA TOKITA - KAZUO YAMASHITA

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:58.750
<i>The look in his eyes hasn't changed...</i>

00:13:58.830 --> 00:14:01.440
BANDO WAS ARRESTED ON
SUSPICION OF ATTACKING YAKUZA OFFICE

00:14:01.540 --> 00:14:03.980
<i>...even though his appearance</i>
<i>is a lot different now.</i>

00:14:04.050 --> 00:14:05.920
<i>That is definitely...</i>

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:09.180
<i>Yohei Bando.</i>

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:11.180
Take your stance.

00:14:14.220 --> 00:14:15.480
Huh?

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:17.060
What's wrong, guys?

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:21.400
I'm not a combat fighter.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:23.320
So, I don't need a stance.

00:14:23.900 --> 00:14:25.820
He's right.

00:14:25.990 --> 00:14:28.700
I'll go with my usual style.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.160
Fine. Have it your way.
Fight!

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:36.540
I don't feel good about this,
but I don't have much choice.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.920
Well, then...

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:41.500
I just need to kill this boy, huh?

00:14:47.470 --> 00:14:50.930
And you said you weren't
a combat fighter?

00:14:51.140 --> 00:14:53.140
You hit my acupuncture points.

00:14:53.810 --> 00:14:57.560
Or was it called <i>Chin Na</i> in martial arts?

00:14:58.350 --> 00:15:00.440
You really are an ex-med school student.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.440
Seems like you did your homework.

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.360
My style uses <i>Lingshu Chin Na</i> techniques.

00:15:07.440 --> 00:15:09.450
<i>What is </i>Lingshu Chin Na<i>?</i>

00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:13.120
<i>It's the oldest form of </i>Chin Na
<i>written in </i>Huangdi Neijing<i>,</i>

00:15:13.240 --> 00:15:15.030
<i>an ancient Chinese medical text.</i>

00:15:15.700 --> 00:15:17.540
<i>Using their fingers as needles,</i>

00:15:17.830 --> 00:15:21.790
<i>fighters strike the human's vital</i>
<i>meridians and acupuncture points.</i>

00:15:22.460 --> 00:15:26.250
<i>It is said that it's easy for</i>
<i>a master of Lingshu Chin Na</i>

00:15:26.340 --> 00:15:29.800
<i>to cripple the opponent</i>
<i>with just a single strike.</i>

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:32.340
How logical.

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:36.350
That's one of the effective means
for you to defeat me,

00:15:36.430 --> 00:15:38.520
someone physically superior to you.

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:39.850
"Means"?

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:42.560
Exactly.

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:46.480
Martial arts are no more than
a means to an end for me.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:51.240
And the end is to dissect your body.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.790
<i>Wow! His hits are incredible.</i>

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:02.210
<i>He's taking advantage of</i>
<i>his small body to make quick moves!</i>

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:07.040
Hanafusa is toying with Bando!

00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.960
Good grief.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:11.510
His small body allows him
to move quickly.

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:13.760
What a pain.

00:16:14.340 --> 00:16:19.140
<i>Any ordinary person wouldn't be able</i>
<i>to fight with that pain.</i>

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:23.730
<i>Are those thick muscles preventing</i>
<i>my strikes from hitting deeply?</i>

00:16:24.270 --> 00:16:26.560
<i>Very interesting.</i>

00:16:27.270 --> 00:16:29.650
<i>I would do anything to dissect him.</i>

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:34.990
I'll keep him as intact as possible.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:37.280
<i>My aim is... your </i>yamen.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:40.290
LINGSHU CHIN NA: TERMINAL STAB

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.830
Now you will never be conscious again.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:48.090
I can enjoy dissecting your body now.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:49.670
Oh?

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:53.510
Open fractures
of the second and third fingers.

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:57.680
Any ordinary person would be
rolling around in pain with those.

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:01.720
It seems you're not normal either.

00:17:02.520 --> 00:17:06.770
In fact, I am also categorized
as "abnormal."

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:08.980
I bet.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:12.240
The cervical vertebrae is
a vital point of the human body.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:15.950
You can't protect it
by just building muscle.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:20.200
There is only one answer to this.

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:21.910
Mr. Bando...

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:27.250
your joints are abnormally flexible,
aren't they?

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:32.170
<i>The instant I struck your </i>yamen<i>,</i>
<i>an acupuncture point on the neck,</i>

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:37.220
<i>you caught and broke my fingers in between</i>
<i>your occipital bone and cervical spine.</i>

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:41.850
I assume your joint motion range
would be approximately 140 degrees.

00:17:42.600 --> 00:17:44.430
Well, Mr. Bando?

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:47.480
Is my inference correct?

00:17:48.600 --> 00:17:50.360
You're impressive.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.440
That is correct.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:58.660
My range of joint motion is far different
from that of an ordinary human.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:00.320
-Mama!
-Eek!

00:18:00.490 --> 00:18:02.910
His neck is twisted upside down!

00:18:03.790 --> 00:18:09.710
Now, let's settle this battle
between abnormal fighters.

00:18:10.880 --> 00:18:16.420
I'm afraid killing is the only way
I know how to defeat.

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:17.550
KOKOMI YOSHIZAWA

00:18:17.630 --> 00:18:18.760
Doctor, run!

00:18:26.180 --> 00:18:27.600
Are you surprised?

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:29.310
This is my...

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.230
ace in the hole.

00:18:34.400 --> 00:18:37.780
Well?
Don't you find their forms exquisite?

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:41.070
It's a sword!

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:47.080
<i>There are something like swords</i>
<i>sticking out of Hanafusa's palms.</i>

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:51.500
These are my favorites
carved out of my own femur.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.670
<i>I did everything from designing</i>
<i>the gimmick, processing the bone,</i>

00:18:55.760 --> 00:18:57.920
<i>and to doing the surgery on my own.</i>

00:18:59.930 --> 00:19:01.340
That was so much fun.

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:03.800
Are those allowed?

00:19:04.350 --> 00:19:06.100
Of course, they are.

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:08.930
These are part of my body.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:12.020
I'm offended if you think
those are weapons.

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:16.680
METSUDO KATAHARA
CHAIRMAN KENGAN ASSOCIATION

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:19.820
Part of his body, he says?
He's got me there.

00:19:21.780 --> 00:19:23.870
<i>I knew it.</i>

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:27.500
<i>First, I noticed it through his reaction</i>
<i>to his fractured fingers.</i>

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.500
<i>And now this gadget.</i>

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:31.750
<i>Mr. Hanafusa,</i>

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:35.420
<i>you don't feel pain, do you?</i>

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:42.840
<i>Just as Bando guesses,</i>
<i>Hajime Hanafusa has no sense of pain.</i>

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:49.180
<i>He conducted a surgery to limit the</i>
<i>neurotransmitter function of hypothalamus</i>

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:53.060
<i>and completely blocked out pain sensation.</i>

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:54.900
<i>Which means...</i>

00:19:55.650 --> 00:19:59.650
<i>Hajime Hanafusa cannot be defeated</i>
<i>without getting killed.</i>

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:05.450
<i>Jeez.</i>

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:07.950
<i>What a man.</i>

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:13.460
I’m getting excited to meet
someone similar to me.

00:20:14.040 --> 00:20:17.420
I don't care about
winning or losing anymore, but...

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:20.720
this excitement is quite addicting.

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:22.930
Mr. Bando,

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:26.930
could you die for my pleasure?

00:20:30.560 --> 00:20:34.940
<i>By his power... and that blast sound...</i>

00:20:35.770 --> 00:20:38.480
<i>has he injected compressed gas</i>
<i>into his heels?</i>

00:20:43.950 --> 00:20:47.410
I recommend you go see a doctor
for your mental health,

00:20:47.620 --> 00:20:50.080
if you survive this fight.

00:20:50.620 --> 00:20:52.460
That's insulting.

00:20:52.710 --> 00:20:54.620
I am a doctor, you know?

00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:58.500
I'm fully capable of diagnosing
my own mental state.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.010
Objectively speaking,

00:21:03.590 --> 00:21:06.010
I am far from normal!

00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:11.060
That's what I thought.

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:24.320
<i>It's...</i>

00:21:24.530 --> 00:21:26.530
<i>It's over!</i>

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:31.490
<i>Bando snapped Hanafusa's neck!</i>

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:37.750
<i>We are not sure if</i>
<i>Hanafusa is still alive.</i>

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:40.340
<i>That was close.</i>

00:21:41.130 --> 00:21:44.760
<i>He tried to stab me in the solar plexus.</i>

00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:47.340
<i>It was a good call.</i>

00:21:47.970 --> 00:21:51.680
<i>Attacks to my midsection</i>
<i>are very difficult to dodge,</i>

00:21:52.100 --> 00:21:57.390
<i>especially when it's in the center</i>
<i>of my body, like the solar plexus.</i>

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:03.530
<i>If I hadn't quickly shifted my spine,</i>

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:07.740
-<i>I would have been the dead one.</i>
-Bring a stretcher! Quick!

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:14.950
Oh, Bando. Nice work out there.

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:19.710
You are slightly injured,
but it doesn't look severe.

00:22:20.080 --> 00:22:22.630
I hope you keep up the good work
in the next round.

00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:27.220
Stupid Doctor! Why did you die on me?

00:22:27.340 --> 00:22:32.350
I couldn't do anything to thank him
for saving my brother.

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:33.760
KARURA KURE

00:22:33.850 --> 00:22:35.930
Nothing can be done about this, Elena.

00:22:36.000 --> 00:22:39.520
Dead people never come back to life.

00:22:40.060 --> 00:22:42.730
You're in a sorry plight, Hanafusa.

00:22:43.480 --> 00:22:44.690
Mr. Dazai!

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:46.570
How could you say such a thing to him?

00:22:46.740 --> 00:22:51.070
Dr. Hanafusa fought to the death!

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:52.240
Indeed.

00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:56.450
Now, let's find out
if it was worth costing his life.

00:22:56.870 --> 00:22:57.910
What?

00:22:58.410 --> 00:23:00.250
Mr. Dazai?

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:02.840
What are you...

00:23:05.460 --> 00:23:07.840
Phew. I'm back.

00:23:09.680 --> 00:23:12.180
Good grief. I thought I would die.

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:13.600
Doctor!

00:23:13.720 --> 00:23:16.430
What? Didn't you... die?

00:23:17.430 --> 00:23:20.560
Ms. Yoshizawa,
you know I'm a doctor, right?

00:23:20.850 --> 00:23:25.320
I remodeled my body,
just in case I was to die,

00:23:26.070 --> 00:23:30.400
implanting a medical device
to force my heart to beat.

00:23:30.570 --> 00:23:33.370
Oh, I see.

00:23:33.570 --> 00:23:35.590
I have no energy left to question anymore.

00:23:36.040 --> 00:23:38.700
But honestly,

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:43.580
one more twist to my vertebrae
would have killed me.

00:23:43.830 --> 00:23:46.960
So, Hanafusa. How did it go?

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:50.510
Don't worry.

00:23:51.050 --> 00:23:53.090
Yohei Bando...

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:57.220
will be a dead man shortly.

00:23:58.640 --> 00:24:00.020
What's wrong, Bando?

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:02.270
<i>He got me.</i>

00:24:02.850 --> 00:24:06.480
<i>That man surprises me till the end.</i>

00:24:07.610 --> 00:24:09.610
<i>What he said at that moment...</i>

00:24:10.280 --> 00:24:13.780
I don't care about
winning or losing anymore.

00:24:13.910 --> 00:24:19.950
<i>At that time, I thought it was just</i>
<i>an expression of his berserker nature.</i>

00:24:20.620 --> 00:24:22.830
<i>However, the true meaning</i>
<i>of his statement was</i>

00:24:22.920 --> 00:24:27.630
<i>that he had completed</i>
<i>his arrangement to kill me.</i>

00:24:28.090 --> 00:24:29.380
<i>Looking at these symptoms...</i>

00:24:29.840 --> 00:24:32.510
<i>it must be a virus</i>
<i>that attacks the nerves.</i>

00:24:33.090 --> 00:24:36.180
<i>This is a blood-borne infection.</i>

00:24:36.470 --> 00:24:41.930
<i>It must have transmitted through his blood</i>
<i>on his bone blades.</i>

00:24:42.480 --> 00:24:43.440
Yes.

00:24:43.770 --> 00:24:45.310
Prior to the match,

00:24:45.940 --> 00:24:49.900
I injected a lethal virus in myself.

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:53.030
But... wouldn't that kill you, too?

00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:54.950
There's no need to worry.

00:24:55.660 --> 00:24:59.660
I also possess an antibody for the virus.

00:25:00.790 --> 00:25:02.250
<i>I see.</i>

00:25:02.540 --> 00:25:06.880
<i>If I can find out what type of virus</i>
<i>he used, I could cope with this.</i>

00:25:07.080 --> 00:25:11.510
<i>However, I don't think the medical</i>
<i>facility on this small island can do much.</i>

00:25:12.210 --> 00:25:14.550
<i>This was what he wanted, huh?</i>

00:25:15.260 --> 00:25:17.010
<i>Mr. Hanafusa,</i>

00:25:17.090 --> 00:25:21.680
<i>the winner of this battle... is you.</i>

00:25:22.890 --> 00:25:26.900
<i>On this day, after 25 years,</i>

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:31.570
<i>the execution of Yohei Bando</i>
<i>has been successfully carried out.</i>

00:25:36.030 --> 00:25:37.110
PREVIEW

00:25:37.240 --> 00:25:41.740
<i>The dull, skinny, useless mediocre Kaneda</i>
<i>fights against the Thai God of War.</i>

00:25:41.870 --> 00:25:45.130
<i>It's a craving for power.</i>
<i>Don't back off. Don't get frightened.</i>

00:25:45.250 --> 00:25:48.520
<i>There's no reason</i>
<i>the weak can't defeat the strong.</i>

00:25:48.580 --> 00:25:49.750
<i>Next episode: "Volition."</i>

00:25:50.220 --> 00:25:51.860
Subtitle translation by Miki Miyaji
